<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'none'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<title>CONFIDENTIAL — Compromise check: {% if reports|length == 1 %}{{ reports[0].host|visible(80) }}{% else %}{{ reports|length }} hosts{% endif %}</title>
<style>
:root { --ink: #1d232a; --muted: #5b6672; --line: #d6dbe0; --paper: #ffffff; --soft: #f4f6f8;
  --critical: #6a040f; --high: #a4161a; --medium: #b85c00; --low: #44617b; --info: #6b7280; --ok: #2d6a4f; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root { --ink: #e6e9ec; --muted: #a3acb6; --line: #39424c; --paper: #15191d; --soft: #1e242a;
    --critical: #ff8fa3; --high: #ff6b6b; --medium: #ffa94d; --low: #8fb3d9; --info: #a3acb6; --ok: #69db7c; }
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
  font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 16px 48px; }
.banner { background: var(--high); color: #fff; text-align: center; font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: .08em; padding: 6px 16px; position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1; }
h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 24px 0 4px; }
h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 40px 0 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 2px solid var(--line); }
h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 24px 0 8px; }
.meta, .muted { color: var(--muted); }
.notice { background: var(--soft); border-left: 4px solid var(--medium); padding: 10px 14px; margin: 16px 0; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 8px 0; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
td.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.band { display: inline-block; min-width: 4.5em; text-align: center; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 6px;
  font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; }
.band.critical { background: var(--critical); }
.score { font-weight: 700; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; color: #fff; background: var(--low); white-space: nowrap; }
.score.elevated { background: var(--medium); } .score.high { background: var(--high); } .score.critical { background: var(--critical); }
.scoreline { font-size: 1.1rem; } .band.high { background: var(--high); } .band.medium { background: var(--medium); }
.band.low { background: var(--low); } .band.info { background: var(--info); }
.finding { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 12px; margin: 10px 0; }
.finding .title { font-weight: 600; }
.tag { font-size: .75rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 3px; padding: 0 4px; margin-left: 6px; color: var(--muted); }
.evidence { margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: .85rem; }
.evidence td { border: 0; padding: 2px 8px 2px 0; }
code, .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: .85em;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere; word-break: break-word; }
details { margin: 8px 0; } summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); }
.wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
footer { margin-top: 48px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 12px; }
@page { size: A4; margin: 18mm 14mm; @top-center { content: "Confidential"; color: #5b6672; font-size: 9pt; } @bottom-right { content: counter(page) " of " counter(pages); color: #5b6672; font-size: 9pt; } }
@media print { .mono { overflow-wrap: anywhere; } .wrap { overflow: visible; } table { width: 100%; table-layout: auto; } h2, h3 { break-after: avoid; } .finding { break-inside: avoid; } }
@media print { .banner { position: static; } details { display: block; } details > summary { display: none; }
  h2 { break-before: page; } .finding { break-inside: avoid; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="banner">CONFIDENTIAL — handle like the evidence it describes</div>
<main>
<h1>Compromise check report</h1>
<p class="meta">Generated {{ generated_at }} by {{ operator|visible(60) }} on {{ controller|visible(60) }} ·
checker {{ version }} · checks version {{ checks_version }}</p>

<div class="notice">
<p><strong>The probability is an estimate, not a measurement.</strong> Each host's probability of
compromise combines its findings' likelihood ratios with a prior (DESIGN.md §11), and is shown with a
band (Low, Elevated, High, Critical) for that reason. Hygiene and exposure are rated separately and
never move it. Low coverage doesn't lower it: read it beside the coverage section.</p>
<p><strong>No findings is not proof of a clean server.</strong> Attackers can avoid or remove
evidence, logs may be missing, and no set of checks covers every technique. Check the coverage
section for each host. A high band is a reason to investigate, not proof of an intrusion.</p>
<p><strong>Confidential.</strong> This report describes weaknesses an attacker could use. Keep it
with the evidence and share it only with people who need it.</p>
{% if not advisor_enabled %}
<p><strong>AI advisor: off.</strong> The tool can ask an AI model to explain these findings and
suggest next steps; it stays off unless your organization turns it on (security and privacy
policy §9).</p>
{% endif %}
</div>

<h2>Summary</h2>
<div class="wrap"><table>
<tr><th>Host</th><th>Collected</th><th>Bundle</th><th>Probability</th>
<th class="num">Critical</th><th class="num">High</th><th class="num">Medium</th><th class="num">Low</th>
<th class="num">Hygiene</th><th class="num">Exposure</th><th class="num">Coverage gaps</th></tr>
{% for r in reports %}
{% set c = r.counts.get("compromise indicator", {}) %}
<tr>
<td><a href="#host-{{ loop.index }}">{{ r.host|visible(60) }}</a></td>
<td class="mono">{{ r.row["started_at"][:16] }}</td>
<td class="mono">{{ r.row["status"] }}</td>
<td><span class="score {{ r.assessment.score.band|lower }}">{{ r.assessment.score.probability|percent }} {{ r.assessment.score.band }}</span></td>
<td class="num">{{ c.get("critical", 0) }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.get("high", 0) }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.get("medium", 0) }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.get("low", 0) }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ r.counts.get("hygiene", {}).values()|sum }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ r.counts.get("exposure", {}).values()|sum }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ r.assessment.coverage.gaps|length }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>

{% macro advice_meta(x, full=False) %}<p class="meta">Asked {{ x.model_asked|visible(80) }}{% if x.declined_by %}; declined by {{ x.declined_by|join(", ")|visible(200) }}{% endif %}{% if x.model_answered %}; answered by {{ x.model_answered|visible(80) }}{% if x.endpoint %} at {{ x.endpoint|visible(200) }}{% endif %}{% endif %} · redaction {{ x.redaction }} · {{ x.at[:16] }} UTC{% if full %} · about the assessment of {{ x.assessed_at[:16] }}{% endif %}{% if x.stale %} · <strong>stale{% if full %}: it read another collection or assessment of this host than this report shows{% endif %}</strong>{% endif %}</p>
{% if x.warning %}<p><strong>Warning: {{ x.warning|visible(600) }}.</strong></p>{% endif %}
{% if x.local and x.model_answered %}<p class="muted">Answered by a local model, on the machine that ran <span class="mono">checker advise</span>: expect lower quality than from a large hosted model, and read it with more care.</p>{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro came_to_nothing(title, entry) %}{% set x = entry.get("later") %}{% if x %}<p class="muted">AI advisor, {{ title }}: {% if entry.get("answered") %}a later request{% else %}a request{% endif %} ({{ x.model_asked|visible(80) }}, {{ x.at[:16] }} UTC) came to nothing: {{ x.note|visible(400) }}.</p>{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro finding_card(f) %}
<div class="finding">
<div><span class="band {{ f.band }}">{{ f.band|upper }}</span>
<span class="mono muted">F-{{ f.number }}</span>
<span class="title">{{ f.title|visible(200) }}</span>
{% if f.new %}<span class="tag">new</span>{% endif %}
<span class="tag mono">{{ f.check }}</span></div>
<div class="mono">{{ f.summary|visible(400) }}</div>
{% if f.uncertain %}<div class="muted">Uncertain: {{ f.uncertain|visible(300) }}</div>{% endif %}
{% if f.raised_by_pack and not f.maintenance %}<div class="muted">Weighted by threat pack <span class="mono">{{ f.raised_by_pack|visible(160) }}</span>: odds times {{ "%g"|format(f.likelihood_ratio) }} while its threat counts.</div>{% endif %}
{% if f.maintenance %}<div class="muted">In maintenance window <span class="mono">{{ f.maintenance.window|visible(80) }}</span> ({{ f.maintenance.layer|visible(80) }}: {{ f.maintenance.reason|visible(200) }}); {{ f.maintenance.band }} outside it.</div>{% endif %}
{% if f.first_seen %}<div class="muted">Seen {{ f.first_seen[:19] }}{% if f.last_seen and f.last_seen != f.first_seen %} to {{ f.last_seen[:19] }}{% endif %} (controller clock, UTC)</div>{% endif %}
{% if f.excerpts %}
<table class="evidence">
{% for e in f.excerpts %}<tr><td class="mono muted">{{ e.when }}</td><td class="muted">{{ e.where }}</td><td class="mono">{{ e.text }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}
</div>
{% endmacro %}

{% for r in reports %}
<h2 id="host-{{ loop.index }}">{{ r.host|visible(80) }}</h2>
{% set facts = r.manifest.get("host") or {} %}
<p class="meta">Bundle <span class="mono">{{ r.row["id"]|visible(120) }}</span> · collected {{ r.row["started_at"][:19] }} ·
{% if facts.get("os_pretty_name") %}{{ facts["os_pretty_name"]|visible(80) }} · {% endif %}
{% if facts.get("kernel") %}kernel {{ facts["kernel"]|visible(60) }} · {% endif %}
baseline <span class="mono">{{ r.assessment.baseline_id|visible(120) }}</span>{% if r.assessment.baseline_set_now %} (set at this analysis){% endif %}</p>
{% for note in r.assessment.notes %}<div class="notice">{{ note|visible(400) }}</div>{% endfor %}

{% set s = r.assessment.score %}
<h3>Probability of compromise</h3>
<p class="scoreline"><span class="score {{ s.band|lower }}">{{ s.probability|percent }} · {{ s.band }}</span>
<span class="muted">from a prior of {{ s.prior|percent }} ({{ s.prior_source|visible(60) }}){% if s.raised_prior %}, raised to {{ s.raised_prior|percent }} by exposure to {% for b in s.raised_by %}{{ b.pack|visible(80) }} v{{ b.version }} ({{ (b.share * 100)|round|int }}% of its window, at most){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %};
{{ r.assessment.coverage.gaps|length }} coverage gap(s) below. Hygiene and exposure, rated separately: {{ s.hygiene_and_exposure.band }}.</span></p>
{% if s.contributors %}
<div class="wrap"><table>
<tr><th>Contributor</th><th>Check</th><th class="num">Likelihood ratio</th><th class="num">Share</th><th>Capped</th></tr>
{% for c in s.contributors %}
<tr><td>{{ c.title|visible(200) }}{% if c.chain %}<div class="muted">a chain of:
{% for i in c.chain.findings %}{{ r.assessment.findings[i].title|visible(120) }}; {% endfor %}{% for i in c.chain.events %}a login{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}</td><td class="mono">{{ c.check }}</td><td class="num">×{{ "%g"|format(c.ratio) }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ c.share|percent }}</td><td class="muted">{{ c.capped or "" }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<p class="muted">Findings about the same file or process count once in full; one check's repeated findings add at most a doubling;
"capped" marks a finding a cap cut;
uncertain findings count half. Suppressed and informational findings don't count.</p>
{% else %}<p class="muted">No compromise indicators: the probability is the prior{% if s.raised_prior %}, as raised{% endif %}.</p>{% endif %}

<h3>Compromise indicators</h3>
{% set shown = r.findings.get("compromise indicator", [])|rejectattr("band", "equalto", "info")|list %}
{% if shown %}{% for f in shown %}{{ finding_card(f) }}{% endfor %}
{% else %}<p class="muted">None found. See the coverage below for what could not be seen.</p>{% endif %}
{% set infos = r.findings.get("compromise indicator", [])|selectattr("band", "equalto", "info")|list %}
{% if infos %}<details><summary>{{ infos|length }} informational findings (reboots by operators, su use, user units…)</summary>
{% for f in infos %}{{ finding_card(f) }}{% endfor %}</details>{% endif %}

<h3>Exposure and hygiene</h3>
<p class="muted">Risks worth fixing, not evidence that anyone got in (they are reported apart from compromise indicators).</p>
{% set other = r.findings.get("exposure", []) + r.findings.get("hygiene", []) %}
{% if other %}{% for f in other %}{{ finding_card(f) }}{% endfor %}
{% else %}<p class="muted">None found.</p>{% endif %}

<h3>Timeline</h3>
{% if r.timeline %}
<div class="wrap"><table>
<tr><th>When (UTC, controller clock)</th><th>Event</th><th>Finding</th></tr>
{% for e in r.timeline %}<tr><td class="mono">{{ e.when[:19] }}</td><td class="mono">{{ e.type }} · {{ e.text }}</td><td>{{ e.findings|join("; ")|visible(200) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% else %}<p class="muted">No logged events behind the findings.</p>{% endif %}

<h3>Coverage</h3>
{% if r.assessment.coverage.log_reach %}
<table><tr><th>Log</th><th>From</th><th>To</th><th class="num">Days</th></tr>
{% for name, reach in r.assessment.coverage.log_reach.items() %}<tr><td class="mono">{{ name }}</td><td class="mono">{{ reach["from"][:16] }}</td><td class="mono">{{ reach["to"][:16] }}</td><td class="num">{{ reach["days"] }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="muted">From the events the checks use: a quiet log may reach further back.</p>
{% endif %}
{% if r.assessment.coverage.gaps %}<ul>{% for g in r.assessment.coverage.gaps %}<li>{{ g|visible(400) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% else %}<p class="muted">No gaps recorded.</p>{% endif %}
{% set waiting = r.assessment.checks|rejectattr("status", "equalto", "ran")|list %}
{% if waiting %}<p>Checks not run: {% for c in waiting %}<span class="mono">{{ c.check }}</span> ({{ c.status|visible(200) }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
{% set entry = r.advice.get("explain") or {} %}
{% set a = entry.get("answered") or entry.get("later") %}
{% set later = entry.get("later") if entry.get("answered") else None %}
{% if a %}
<h3>AI advisor (advice, not findings)</h3>
<div class="notice">
{{ advice_meta(a, True) }}
{% if a.answer %}
<p><strong>Verdict: {{ a.answer.verdict|visible(80) }}.</strong> {{ a.answer.summary|visible(2000) }}</p>
{% if a.answer.most_important %}<p>Most important:</p><ul>{% for p in a.answer.most_important %}<li><span class="mono">{{ p.finding|visible(20) }}</span>: {{ p.why|visible(1000) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
{% if a.answer.innocent_explanations %}<p>Possible innocent explanations:</p><ul>{% for p in a.answer.innocent_explanations %}<li><span class="mono">{{ p.finding|visible(20) }}</span>: {{ p.explanation|visible(1000) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
{% if a.answer.what_would_settle_it %}<p>What would settle it:</p><ul>{% for q in a.answer.what_would_settle_it %}<li>{{ q|visible(1000) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
{% else %}<p>No advice: {{ a.note|visible(400) }}.</p>{% endif %}
{% if later %}<p class="muted">A later request ({{ later.at[:16] }} UTC) came to nothing: {{ later.note|visible(400) }}.</p>{% endif %}
<p class="muted">Written by an AI model from the findings above; the probability and band are the tool's own and unchanged. Finding numbers (F-n) count the analysis's findings in order.</p>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% set m = (r.advice.get("remediation") or {}).get("answered") %}
{% if m and m.answer %}
<h3>AI advisor: remediation (advice; nothing was run)</h3>
<div class="notice">
{{ advice_meta(m) }}
<p><strong>Urgency: {{ m.answer.urgency|visible(20) }}.</strong> {{ m.answer.summary|visible(2000) }}</p>
{% for title, key in (("Preserve evidence first", "preserve"), ("Contain", "contain"), ("Eradicate", "eradicate"), ("Recover", "recover")) %}
{% if m.answer[key] %}<p>{{ title }}:</p><ol>{% for s in m.answer[key] %}<li><span class="mono">{{ s.action|visible(1000) }}</span>{% if s.destructive %} <strong>[destroys state]</strong>{% endif %}{% if s.findings %} ({{ s.findings|join(", ")|visible(100) }}){% endif %}<div class="muted">Why: {{ s.why|visible(600) }} · Risk: {{ s.risk|visible(400) }}</div></li>{% endfor %}</ol>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if m.answer.tell %}<p>Tell:</p><ul>{% for t in m.answer.tell %}<li>{{ t.role|visible(120) }}: {{ t.what|visible(400) }} ({{ t.when|visible(120) }})</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
<p class="muted">Written by an AI model for a person to weigh against what they know of the host. Commands are shown as text; the tool runs nothing. Preserve evidence before any step marked as destroying state.</p>
</div>
{% endif %}
{{ came_to_nothing("remediation", r.advice.get("remediation") or {}) }}
{% set c = (r.advice.get("coverage") or {}).get("answered") %}
{% if c and c.answer %}
{% set offered = c.answer.judged|selectattr("accepted")|list %}
<h3>AI advisor: coverage suggestions (nothing changed)</h3>
<div class="notice">
{{ advice_meta(c) }}
<p class="muted">As judged against the settings at {{ c.at[:16] }} UTC; a setting changed since may already be in place.</p>
{% if offered %}<ul>{% for j in offered %}<li>{{ j.suggestion.why|visible(600) }}{% for g in j.cited %}<div class="muted">For {{ g|visible(400) }}</div>{% endfor %}<div class="muted">Cost, as the advisor sees it: {{ j.suggestion.trade_off|visible(300) }}</div>{% if j.note %}<div><strong>{{ j.note|visible(1000) }}</strong></div>{% endif %}<div class="mono">{{ j.action|visible(1000) }}</div></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% else %}<p>No suggestions offered.</p>{% endif %}
{% set aside = c.answer.judged|rejectattr("accepted")|list %}
{% if aside %}<p class="muted">{{ aside|length }} set aside: {% for j in aside %}{{ j.reason|visible(200) }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endif %}
{{ came_to_nothing("coverage suggestions", r.advice.get("coverage") or {}) }}
{% set w = (r.advice.get("whitelist") or {}).get("answered") %}
{% if w and w.answer %}
{% set offered = w.answer.judged|selectattr("accepted")|list %}
<h3>AI advisor: whitelist proposals (not in effect)</h3>
<div class="notice">
{{ advice_meta(w) }}
<p>{{ offered|length }} proposed{% if w.answer.file %}, written to <span class="mono">{{ w.answer.file|visible(300) }}</span> for a person to review{% endif %}; {{ w.answer.judged|length - offered|length }} set aside.</p>
{% if w.answer.judged %}<ul>{% for j in w.answer.judged %}<li><span class="mono">{{ j.id|visible(80) }}</span>: {% if j.accepted %}hides {{ j.hides|join("; ")|visible(600) }}{% else %}set aside: {{ j.reason|visible(300) }}{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
<p class="muted">A proposal is only offered when it hides exactly the findings it names, none of them critical or part of a chain. Nothing changes until a person copies a rule into the whitelist.</p>
</div>
{% endif %}
{{ came_to_nothing("whitelist proposals", r.advice.get("whitelist") or {}) }}
{% endfor %}

<h2>Appendix</h2>
{% for r in reports %}
{% set w = r.assessment.whitelist %}
<h3>{{ r.host|visible(80) }}: suppressed findings</h3>
{% if not w %}<p class="muted">No whitelist applied.</p>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">Whitelist <span class="mono">{{ w.hash[:16] }}</span>: {{ w.rules|length }} rule(s){% if w.disabled %}, {{ w.disabled|length }} switched off{% endif %}.
Suppressed findings are kept, here, and count for nothing in the probability.</p>
{% if w.expired %}<div class="notice">Expired rules, no longer applied: {% for e in w.expired %}<span class="mono">{{ e|visible(120) }}</span>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
{% if r.suppressed %}
<div class="wrap"><table>
<tr><th>Band</th><th>Finding</th><th>Rule</th><th>Reason</th><th>Owner</th></tr>
{% for f in r.suppressed %}
<tr><td><span class="band {{ f.band }}">{{ f.band|upper }}</span></td>
<td><span class="mono muted">F-{{ f.number }}</span> {{ f.title|visible(200) }}<div class="mono muted">{{ f.summary|visible(300) }}</div></td>
<td class="mono">{{ f.suppressed_by.layer|visible(80) }} / {{ f.suppressed_by.rule|visible(80) }}</td>
<td>{{ f.suppressed_by.reason|visible(300) }}</td><td>{{ f.suppressed_by.owner|visible(80) }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% else %}<p class="muted">No finding matched a rule.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% for r in reports %}
<h3>{{ r.host|visible(80) }}: collection and custody</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Bundle</th><td class="mono">{{ r.row["id"]|visible(120) }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Status</th><td>{{ r.row["status"] }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Collected</th><td class="mono">{{ r.row["started_at"] }} to {{ r.row["ended_at"] }} (controller clock)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Collector</th><td class="mono">version {{ r.row["collector_version"]|visible(40) }}, SHA-256 {{ r.row["collector_sha256"] }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Content</th><td class="mono">{{ r.row["plaintext_bytes"] }} bytes, SHA-256 {{ r.row["plaintext_sha256"] }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Encrypted file</th><td class="mono">{{ r.row["ciphertext_bytes"] }} bytes, SHA-256 {{ r.row["ciphertext_sha256"] }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Host</th><td class="mono">{{ r.manifest.get("host", {})|visible(400) }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Modules</th><td class="mono">{{ r.manifest.get("modules_planned", [])|join(", ") }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Masking</th><td>version {{ r.manifest.get("masking_version") }}: secrets were masked on the server before anything left it</td></tr>
<tr><th>Analysis</th><td class="mono">{{ r.assessment.analysed_at }}, checks version {{ r.assessment.checks_version }}</td></tr>
</table>
<details open><summary>Chain of custody ({{ r.custody|length }} entries)</summary>
<div class="wrap"><table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>When (UTC)</th><th>Action</th><th>Who</th><th>From</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
{% for c in r.custody %}<tr><td class="num">{{ c["seq"] }}</td><td class="mono">{{ c["at"][:19] }}</td><td>{{ c["action"] }}</td><td>{{ c["operator"]|visible(60) }}</td><td>{{ c["controller"]|visible(60) }}</td><td class="mono">{{ (c["detail"] or "")|visible(200) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>
</details>
{% endfor %}

<footer>
